senses.gloss:
तरण्ड, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, m. f. n. a boat, a vessel;
(अस्, अम्), m. n. a raft or float made of bamboos &c.
tied together and sometimes floated upon jars or
hollow gourds inverted; the float of a fishing line;
an oar; (अस्), m., N. of a country; [cf. the following.]
—तरण्ड-पादा, f. a boat, a ship.

तरीष, अस्, m. a raft, a float, a boat; the ocean;
a fit or competent person; a fine shape or form; deco-
rating, ornamenting; practice, business, profession;
heaven or paradise; (ई), f., N. of a daughter of Indra.

1. तरु, उस्, उस्, उ, = तरणि, Ved. passing through;
(Sāy.) rapid motion, velocity; a wooden ladle for
taking up the Soma; [cf. 2. तरु next col.]

तरुतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. overcoming, conquer-
ing, a conqueror; impelling, causing to be quick;
[cf. तरितृ.]

तरम्बुज तरम्बुज, अम्, n. a water-melon,
(most probably borrowed from the Persian تربز);
[cf. also खर्वूज.]

तर्मन् तर्मन्, अ, n. (perhaps fr. rt. तॄ),
the top or end of the sacrificial post; [cf. सु-तर्मन्;
cf. also Gr. τέρμα; Lat. terminus.]

तर्ष 2. तर्ष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तृष्), thirst;
wish, desire; Desire personified as a son of Arka
(the sun) and Vāsanā.
